sentences.l:
But come, suitors, since this contest has appeared,
such as now there is not a woman throughout the Achaean country,
neither of sacred Pylos nor of Argos nor of Mycenae;
nor of Ithaca itself nor of the dark mainland;

First the axes he set up, a trench having dug through
for all, one long one, and to the line he made them straight,
and around them the earth he packed down;

And Leiodes first rose up, Oenops’ son,
who was their sacrificing-priest, and by the mixing-bowl, the fair one,
sat innermost always;

but when he has tried the bow and seen it,
some other one then of the fair-robed Achaean women
let him woo with bridal gifts, seeking her;

So he spoke, and he quickly kindled up, Melanthius, an untiring fire,
and beside it, bringing, he set a stool, and a fleece upon it,
and out of the tallow he brought a great wheel, that was within;
